{
  "id": "ticket_01KY93E2ZK6Z3TFEBP86ATMW37",
  "name": "transcript capture: move the copy outside the db lock and stream instead of buffering",
  "slug": "transcript-capture-move-the-copy-outside-the-db-lock-and-str",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "captureTranscript does readFile(whole file)+atomicWriteFile INSIDE withLock before any assertHeld, so a large transcript (tens–hundreds of MB) holds the exclusive lock long enough to time out a different concurrent command (default 5s) into a CONFLICT — a lost state change for the neighbor. It also buffers the entire file as one string (size ceiling → silent transcript_ref:null).",
    "details_md": "The never-block guarantee holds for the capturing command but is not transitively true for concurrent neighbors in the multi-agent-same-cwd scenario the design targets.",
    "acceptance": [
      "Transcript locate+copy runs OUTSIDE withLock (its result is only folded into the subsequent session write), or is bounded and guarded by assertHeld immediately before/after",
      "The copy streams source->temp->rename instead of buffering the full file as a string (removing the memory spike and size ceiling)",
      "A test with a large transcript asserts a concurrent command on another ticket is not starved into CONFLICT"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/sessions/transcript.ts:500-505 (readFile+atomicWriteFile, buffered)",
      "callers: stop.ts:77-83, done.ts:120-126, review.ts:151-157, drop.ts:111-117 (inside withLock, before assertHeld)",
      "src/repo/lock.ts:140 default 5s acquire timeout"
    ],
    "meta": {},
    "v": 1
  },
